From 7066b30a7d2681d9039a5fbe1def15f6c6091453 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:19:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strings: the help of the Hades settings in plain language, in
 English and Spanish

The help of the settings that Hades adds said what the program does inside
(InfoFrames, planes, layers, reshaping) and was hard to follow for anyone who
had not read the documentation. Each text now says what changes on the screen
or in the sound, when a person would want it, what the default is and what to
do if the picture goes wrong; the details of the expert settings stay, after
that. Labels that were cryptic are renamed: Dolby Vision Low-Latency "player-led"
(for TVs in game mode), "trims", "content mapping v4.0", "HDR10 as Dolby Vision,
measured", and the values of the v4.0 setting say what each one does.

The messages about the Java menus of Blu-ray discs named the BD-J service and
libbluray; they now say what is wrong in words, and the one about the sound of
an output no longer says "Kodi".

New texts: the Restart entry of the power menu (Estuary 32501), the playback mode
notice (core 41101-41103, Estuary 32502-32504) and the headings of the three new
groups of System > Display (core 41104-41106, Estuary 32505-32507); and the text of
"HDR at more than 8 bits" gets its Estuary strings (32510, 32511), so that it has a
Spanish text too. Setting ids and string ids of the existing texts do not change.
