 msgctxt "#39998"
-msgid "Brightness of the menus, the OSD and text subtitles while the TV is in HDR10, HLG or Dolby Vision mode, relative to the BT.2408 reference white (100 % = 203 nits, as in Kodi). Image subtitles made in HDR (UHD Blu-ray) keep their own levels. The video is never changed."
+msgid "How bright the menus, the on-screen controls and the text subtitles are while the TV is in HDR or Dolby Vision. 100 % is the standard level (white at 203 nits). Lower it if they look too bright on your TV. The video itself never changes, and image subtitles made for HDR keep their own levels."
