 #. Hades, help of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvstepmode"; the core string #39963
 msgctxt "#31748"
-msgid "Where the graphics card cannot prepare a native Dolby Vision picture in the time of a frame, even drawn the faster way and a frame ahead (an integrated one with 4K Blu-ray video and its enhancement layer), the picture can be rebuilt a little less precisely: some of its planes are scaled up with a simpler filter. In test pictures most of the pixels that change do so by the smallest step of a 12-bit picture, none by more than 16 before the last step, which can move a few pixels at edges of strong colour further. Automatic: one step at a time and only as far as the video needs to play smoothly; graphics that keep up always show the exact picture, and what is found is kept for this graphics card and build. Never: always the exact picture, even if the video stutters. Level 1, 2, 3: that level for every frame, to measure what it saves. A level changes only the frames that the renderer says it changes (with the composer of the specification, levels 1 and 2 only those that rebuild the residual of a full enhancement layer, FEL; with libplacebo's reshaping, levels 2 and 3; a picture scaled to the screen, such as a 1080p video, goes out converted to BT.2020 from level 1 on, as earlier builds sent it), and a frame that it does not change is drawn at the highest level under it that changes it, or exactly, as the player information then says. While a level is set nothing that is measured is kept. A level set in advancedsettings.xml (dvstepdown) comes first. Applies from the next video."
+msgid "For experts. Where the graphics card cannot prepare a Dolby Vision picture in the time of a frame, even drawn the faster way and a frame ahead (typically an integrated one with 4K Blu-ray video that has an enhancement layer), the picture can be rebuilt slightly less precisely, with a simpler filter on some planes. In test pictures most changed pixels differ by the smallest step of a 12-bit picture. Automatic (the default): one step at a time and only as far as the video needs to play smoothly; graphics that keep up always show the exact picture, and what is found is kept for this card and build. Never: always the exact picture, even if the video stutters. Level 1, 2, 3: that level on every frame, to measure what it saves; nothing measured is kept meanwhile. A level set in advancedsettings.xml (dvstepdown) comes first. Takes effect from the next video."
 msgstr ""
 
