-msgid "For experts. Where a picture is mapped to the display or to SDR (Dolby Vision or HDR10 on an SDR output, Dolby Vision as HDR10 mapped to the display, Low-Latency), the colours that the display cannot show are mapped through a table. On: a table about three times as fine in brightness and in saturation, closer to the mapping computed exactly (in test pictures the errors of 99.9 % of the pixels are about a third as large, the largest about half), which takes about 201 MB of the graphics card's memory instead of 25 MB and longer to make when a video starts (a third of a second on a fast processor, a few seconds on a slow one). Where it cannot be made, the standard one is used; the log says which one is in use. Applies from the next video."
+msgid "For experts. Where a picture is mapped to the display or to SDR (Dolby Vision or HDR10 on an SDR output, Dolby Vision as HDR10 mapped to the display, Low-Latency), the colours that the display cannot show are mapped through a table. On: a table about three times as fine, closer to the exactly computed mapping (in test pictures the errors of 99.9 % of the pixels are about a third as large), which takes about 201 MB of graphics memory instead of 25 MB and longer to make when a video starts (a third of a second on a fast processor, a few seconds on a slow one). Where it cannot be made, the standard one is used; the log says which. Takes effect from the next video."
