+msgid "On (the default): sound that Hades decodes goes out in no more channels of PCM than your display says it takes (read from its EDID), whatever 'Number of channels' says. A TV that declares stereo gets stereo, and one that declares 6 channels gets 5.1. This avoids silence from multichannel tracks that the display cannot take. Off: decoded sound follows 'Number of channels' alone, for a display that takes more channels than it declares. Passthrough is not affected."
