 #. Hades: setting help: with Dolby Vision and HDR10+ in one video (core #40995)
 msgctxt "#32421"
-msgid "For a video that has both Dolby Vision and HDR10+ metadata of its own, on a display that takes both. Dolby Vision (the default) plays it as before. HDR10+ sends its base layer, the HDR10 picture, with its own HDR10+ metadata, picture by picture; its Dolby Vision is left aside, the enhancement layer of a profile 7 video too. Only for videos whose base layer is HDR10 (profile 7 from a Blu-ray disc, and 8.1). On a display that does not take both, nothing changes. Applies from the next video; for one video, \"Dolby Vision output (this video)\" in its video settings can choose either."
+msgid "For a video that carries both Dolby Vision and HDR10+ data, on a display that takes both. Dolby Vision (the default): plays it as Dolby Vision. HDR10+: sends its HDR10 picture with its HDR10+ data, picture by picture, and leaves its Dolby Vision aside, including the enhancement layer of a profile 7 video. Only for videos whose base layer is HDR10 (profile 7 from a Blu-ray disc, and 8.1). On a display that does not take both, nothing changes. For one video, 'Dolby Vision output (this video)' in its video settings can choose either. Takes effect from the next video."
 msgstr ""
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
@@ -3184,7 +3184,7 @@ msgstr ""
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 #. Hades, help of setting "audiooutput.hadesdialnorm"; the core string #39761
 msgctxt "#32361"
-msgid "Off (as Kodi): the receiver lowers the sound by as much as the dialogue normalisation of the stream says (a Dolby stream at -27 dB plays 4 dB lower). On: in AC-3, E-AC-3 and DTS that are passed through, the dialogue normalisation says 0 dB, and the receiver does not lower the sound; nothing else of the sound changes. It is not what the stream asks for: the volume is set on the receiver. Left as the stream says: Dolby Atmos in E-AC-3 (changing its frames could break its objects), TrueHD (nothing public describes its dialogue normalisation), and DTS whose encoder version cannot say 0 dB. Applies at once; the log says what was changed."
+msgid "Off (the default, as in Kodi): your receiver lowers the sound by as much as the stream's dialogue normalisation says (a Dolby stream at -27 dB plays 4 dB lower). On: in AC-3, E-AC-3 and DTS that are passed through, the dialogue normalisation says 0 dB, and the receiver does not lower the sound; nothing else of the sound changes. This is not what the stream asks for: set the volume on the receiver. Left as the stream says: Dolby Atmos in E-AC-3 (changing its frames could break its objects), TrueHD, and DTS whose encoder version cannot say 0 dB. Takes effect at once; the log says what was changed."
 msgstr ""
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
@@ -3196,7 +3196,7 @@ msgstr ""
